      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:55aovs'
    '|b||Pick the groups by coin flip, and that second term is zero on average.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1njq02m'
    '|a||Without a coin, as in natural data, you have to argue it away.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1og0dmf'
    '|b||Twenty-eight in the lab, zero at the bus stop. In 2007 Steven Levitt and John List argued that gaps like this are no accident.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||In the lab someone is watching, the stakes are small, the setting is strange, and the people chose to come.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1nkgprc'
    '|b||List had seen it on the same card-show floors he''d long studied. Dealers who repaid a generous buyer in a lab version gave lower quality on the show floor, unless they were locals with a reputation to keep.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1v5lo66'
    '|a||Colin Camerer replied that the lab never promised to measure how generous the world is. Its job is to test principles: what pushes giving up or down.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ilslhj'
    '|b||And he found no replicated case of the lab failing when lab and field were closely matched.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ae9et6'
    '|a||Axel Franzen and Sonja Pointner tested it on the same people. They played a dictator game in the lab; weeks later, a misdirected letter with money inside reached their mailbox.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1e21jxj'
    '|b||Those who had given something in the lab returned the letter more often than those who gave nothing. Levels may not travel, as the bus stop showed, but the ranking did.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1b3tonl'
    '|a||And the field has a blind spot of its own: the bus stop is one city, one year, one kind of stranger. That is an external-validity problem too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1y2bh6i'
    '|b||How sure are we? That each method trades control for realism, and the best answers combine them: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1fm54no'
    '|a||How far the lab''s numbers carry into the world: contested, and argued one study at a time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1vjnwln'
    '|a||Three new cases. A library texts a randomly chosen half of its overdue borrowers a reminder. Nobody is told it''s a study. What kind of test is it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1rvuwfd'
    '|a||A natural field experiment: a change assigned at random, in real life, to people who don''t know.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Students in a lab give 30% to a charity, knowing the researcher sees it. A charity plans its mailing on that number. The biggest worry?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||External validity: the cause is clear in the lab, but being watched may not travel to a letter opened at home.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Towns that chose a sugar tax drink less soda than towns that didn''t. The main worry?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5040
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Internal validity: the towns chose the tax, and health-minded towns may drink less soda anyway.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So how do we test a theory of choice? With all three: the lab to find the cause, the field to see if it survives, natural data to see how big it is in the wild.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And when they disagree, as at the bus stop, the gap is a finding in itself. It shows what the lab left out.':
